34,2,,status,Minako,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Minato,,The treasurer logged six hours a month chasing individual payments. That is unsustainable.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The ledger shows seventy percent of costs are fixed, like hall hire. We pay whether we come or not.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Minako,,The sign-in sheets show a quarter of members do two-thirds of the work. That is a huge gap.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,May,,"Since the summer outings had a charge, weekday turnout dropped by a third. People stopped feeling it was theirs.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,The rota confirms it. The same nine people set up and lock up. They are the most active.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@Ryuji, if costs are fixed, why do we chase individual payments? It’s a nightmare.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Minato, because the bank statements show a third of renewals needed reminders. It’s messy.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Shunichi, that imbalance is dangerous. If the active members feel exploited, they will leave.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,May,,"@Minako, I agree. The winter social notes say quiet members feel uneasy about the cost per visit.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, unease is an understatement. It’s being said openly now. We need a fairer system.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Minato,,"@Ryuji, a flat fee might be the only way to stop the chasing. One payment, done.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Minato, a flat fee is risky if costs rise. But activity-based charging creates more admin.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Minako,,"@Ryuji, tiered membership could work. Let people choose their level of involvement.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,May,,"@Minako, tiers might feel exclusive. I worry it will make the quiet members feel like outsiders.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, tiers are better than nothing. At least it acknowledges that not everyone does the same.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Minato,,I prefer the flat fee. It’s simple and stops the endless chasing.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"I am cautious. A flat fee is predictable, but we must ensure it covers the fixed costs.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Minako,,I lean towards tiers. It gives people a choice and respects their different levels of participation.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,May,,I am worried about tiers. I think a flat fee is safer for keeping everyone included.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,I support tiers. It’s the only way to address the imbalance without punishing the active.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
